# Retrieving Interfaces from a GraphQL Endpoint

You can retrieve interfaces using **GraphQL Introspection**. Here are several methods:

---

## 1. Introspection Query (Direct)

```graphql
query GetInterfaces {
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      description
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
          kind
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
        kind
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Filter specifically for INTERFACE types:

```graphql
query GetInterfaces {
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      description
      fields {
        name
        description
        type {
          name
          kind
          ofType {
            name
            kind
          }
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name  # types that implement this interface
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> Then filter results where `kind === "INTERFACE"`

---

## 2. Using curl

```bash
curl -X POST https://your-endpoint/graphql \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "query": "{ __schema { types { kind name possibleTypes { name } } } }"
  }' | jq '.data.__schema.types[] | select(.kind == "INTERFACE")'
```

---

## 3. Using JavaScript/Fetch

```javascript
const fetchInterfaces = async (endpoint) => {
  const query = `
    query {
      __schema {
        types {
          kind
          name
          description
          fields {
            name
            type { name kind }
          }
          possibleTypes {
            name
          }
        }
      }
    }
  `;

  const response = await fetch(endpoint, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ query }),
  });

  const { data } = await response.json();

  // Filter only INTERFACE types
  const interfaces = data.__schema.types.filter(
    (type) => type.kind === 'INTERFACE'
  );

  return interfaces;
};
```

---

## 4. Using GraphQL Tools / CLI

### **graphql-inspector**
```bash
npx graphql-inspector introspect https://your-endpoint/graphql
```

### **get-graphql-schema**
```bash
npx get-graphql-schema https://your-endpoint/graphql
```

### **Apollo Rover CLI**
```bash
rover graph introspect https://your-endpoint/graphql
```

---

## 5. Using GraphiQL / Playground

In **GraphiQL** or **Apollo Sandbox**, use the **Docs/Schema Explorer** panel to browse interfaces visually, or run the introspection query directly.

---

## Example Response

```json
{
  "kind": "INTERFACE",
  "name": "Node",
  "description": "An object with an ID",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "id",
      "type": { "name": "ID", "kind": "SCALAR" }
    }
  ],
  "possibleTypes": [
    { "name": "User" },
    { "name": "Post" }
  ]
}
```

---

## Quick Reference

| Method | Best For |
|--------|----------|
| Introspection Query | Programmatic access |
| curl + jq | Quick CLI inspection |
| JS Fetch | App integration |
| Rover/CLI tools | DevOps/CI pipelines |
| GraphiQL | Visual exploration |

> **Note:** Some production APIs **disable introspection** for security. In that case, you'd need schema documentation or SDL files provided by the API owner.

